# TASK-ARCH-005 (RISK_REGISTER.md R16): Stancl\Tenancy\Bootstrappers\
# FilesystemTenancyBootstrapper (config/tenancy.php, 'suffix_storage_path' =>
# true) creates a real, separate storage_path() subtree per tenant at runtime
# - e.g. storage/tenant{tenant-id}/{app,framework,logs}/... - the exact same
# kind of generated runtime content storage/framework/cache/data/.gitignore
# etc. already exclude for the central app, just not a path stock Laravel's
# own .gitignore anticipates. Never commit tenant runtime storage.
/storage/tenant*/
/test-results

# TASK-OPS-MONITORING-001. config/platform-backup.php's BACKUP_ROOT and
# config/platform-monitoring.php's MONITOR_STATE_PATH both default (when
# unset in .env, e.g. plain local dev) to a path derived from storage_path()
# that resolves under the repo root itself in this Sail-mounted local
# environment - a real backup/monitoring-state directory, never meant to be
# tracked, the exact same class of generated-runtime-content exclusion as
# storage/tenant*/ above. Production always sets BACKUP_ROOT=/backups (a
# dedicated bind mount outside the app source tree entirely - see
# docs/implementation/backup-and-recovery.md), so this only ever matters
# for local testing.
/backups/
/vendor
yarn.lock
yarn-error.log
